2026-09-22: WI-C4c-01 Done: NIF 10.1 KF block decoding in Panopticon.FileFormats.Nif. New blocks: NiControllerSequence (name, accumulation-root name, text-keys ref, controlled blocks as target-name/controller-ref pairs), NiTextKeyExtraData (name + (time, label) keys), NiKeyframeController (next/flags/frequency/phase/start/stop/target/data), NiKeyframeData (linear quaternion rotation keys, or XYZ Euler as order word + three float key groups, then Vector3 translation group + float scale group). New NifKeys.cs: NifKeyType enum (Linear 1/Quadratic 2/Tbc 3/XyzRotation 4/Constant 5), NifKey<T> (forward/backward tangents only on quadratic keys), NifQuaternionKey, NifKeyGroup<T>, internal NifKeyGroupReader (float/vector3 groups return null when empty; unknown type word or Tbc/Constant/non-linear quaternion => NotSupportedException naming block+field; XYZ rotation count must be 1). NifFile dispatch + ValidateReferences: text-keys ref must be NifTextKeyExtraData, controlled-block controller ref must be NifKeyframeController, controller data ref must be NifKeyframeData (InvalidDataException with block index + actual type). NifTestKeyframe test builders incl. key-type overrides for rejection tests; 11 NifKeyframeTests (full clip round-trip incl. empty Roots, quadratic tangent fidelity, empty groups, three bad-ref rejections, Tbc/Constant/unknown/quadratic-quaternion rejections). One pre-existing test updated: NifSceneGraphTests.UnknownBlockTypeFailsNamingBlockAndIndex used NiKeyframeController as its unknown-type fixture, now uses NiMorphData. Also fixed pre-existing main brace-rule violations in ZipFileSystem.cs (3 blank lines, separate commit) so the phase CI can pass. WI-C4c-03 flipped to Ready. Validation: 11/11 new tests, full non-interactive suites green (1480+320+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-03 Done: pure NIF key-curve evaluation in Panopticon.Simulation/Content/Importing/Nif. NifKeyCurve.Evaluate(NifKeyGroup<NifKey<float>>, time): end-held linear/Hermite evaluation, segment-normalized Hermite with outgoing = first key backward and incoming = second key forward (NifSkope convention). NifRotationSampler.EulerToMatrix(x,y,z) returns the stored NifMatrix33 layout for column-vector Rz*Ry*Rx; SampleXyz(data, duration) builds the 6.3 time set (k/30 grid, duration, every source key time; deduped within 1e-6 s), evaluates the three Euler axes, composes via EulerToMatrix, converts to source-frame quaternions (positional transpose before CreateFromRotationMatrix since Matrix4x4 is row-vector), hemisphere-flips consecutive samples, and rejects steps >= 90 degrees (NotSupportedException naming angle + time). 7 NifKeyCurveTests: EulerToMatrix(2.3865, 0.5080, -1.1135) matches the real R_OAR14 stored rest matrix (dumped from nwg1_galley.nifcache) to 2e-4; three-turn linear spin => 31 samples at 36-degree steps in one direction (last sample is negative identity, compared via |dot|); Hermite midpoint vs hand-computed value; linear holds; single-key constant; time-set coverage exactly once; 90-degree step rejected. Validation: 7/7 new tests, full non-interactive suites green (1487+320+53), format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-02 Done: NIF node hierarchy preserved as engine bones. NifSceneConverter now returns internal NifSceneGraph(skeleton, subObjects): every unit-scale NiNode/NiLODNode becomes an ImportedBone depth-first root first (source names, nearest bone ancestor as parent, Galley 30 / Bomber 22 bones, skeleton origin Embedded); bone locals are the source locals conjugated by the source-to-engine map via new NifTransformConverter.CreateBoneLocalMatrix/ConjugateSourceToEngine (A = E^-1 L E; rotation conjugated by Rz90, translation rotated into feet), quaternion sign canonicalized like glTF. Shapes bake their transform RELATIVE to the parent bone (local*relativeToBone)*E, so composing bone rests reproduces the exact C4a world bake (E^-1 W_bone E * relative * E = W_shape * E); non-unit-scale nodes (and their whole subtrees) never become bones and bake into the nearest bone ancestor; a shape with no unit-scale ancestor throws NotSupportedException. NifModelImporter.ImportModel/ImportSkeleton share ReadNifFile; default single-bone skeleton removed. StandaloneModelCapture.ComputeEnclosingBoundingBox now accumulates rest-pose bone worlds (bones are parent-first) instead of using the local-only bone matrix, which is wrong under a real hierarchy. Tests: synthetic importer tests updated + 3 new (hierarchy/conjugation parity incl. real R_OAR14 rest matrix to 1e-4, scaled-subtree collapse, scaled-root rejection); Ee2NifImportTests single-bone asserts replaced with 30/22 bone locks (R_OAR14, prop_01, prop_02, sub-object parents), AssertBounds now computes the exact world AABB from baked vertices transformed by the accumulated bone rest chain (box-corner transforms overestimate rotated sub-objects and would break the locked 0.2 ft AABBs); NifTestBlocks.Node gained a rotation parameter. Static capture parity: Ee2NifProof regenerated on both old and new code; images differ by 0.8-2.5% edge pixels (threshold 12) with a 2px camera recenter from the corrected bounds, same chroma mix, identical validation guides. WI-C4c-04 flipped to Ready (02+03 done). Validation: 13/13 NifModelImporterTests, 4/4 Ee2NifImportTests (interactive), full non-interactive suites green (1472+320+53), format clean, brace check clean except pre-existing ZipFileSystem lines fixed on the group-1 branch.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-04 Done: NIF KF animation importer in Panopticon.Simulation/Content/Importing/Nif. NifAnimationKey parses <model-key>#kf=<archive-relative-kf-path> (null for malformed); NifAnimationImporter (IAnimationImporter, id NIF) resolves the model nifcache + the KF entry through the import FS (null when either is missing), buffers via MemoryStream, requires block 0 to be a controller sequence (InvalidDataException with the asset key), builds the skeleton through the card-02 ConvertGraph entry point, and names the animation after the KF stem. NifAnimationConverter enforces the full section 7 contract: exactly 'start'@0 + 'end'@D>0 text keys (duration from them), key times finite/in-range/non-decreasing at 1e-4, controller flags 0x2C + frequency 1 + phase 0 + null next/target refs, case-insensitive bone targets with duplicate/missing rejection, unit-scale validation (keys within 1e-4 of 1, then dropped), accumulation-root constancy within 1e-5 (ordinary channels when constant, NotSupportedException when varying). Channels: quaternion keys at source key times, XYZ via NifRotationSampler.SampleXyz at the resampled times, translation as X/Y/Z float channels, all Linear; rest-relative offsets follow the C4 rule with one deliberate deviation from the deep-dive's glTF-borrowed phrasing: rotation offset = Concatenate(sample, Inverse(rest)) (NOT Concatenate(Inverse(rest), sample)) because the runtime applies the offset BEFORE the rest (ModelBoneInstance.Matrix = offset * rest) and 'offset * rest == sample' is the locked acceptance criterion; translation offset = (sample - rest) rotated by Inverse(restRotation), matching glTF exactly. Also fixed the latent card-03 transpose bug: NifRotationSampler.ToQuaternion now positionally copies NifMatrix33 into Matrix4x4 (row-vector consistency), and the spin-test direction assertion flipped accordingly (stored Rz*Ry*Rx row-vector = negative axis-angle in System.Numerics). 29 NifAnimationImporterTests (offset reconstruction to 1e-4 against the real R_OAR14 rest, every rejection branch, malformed/missing nulls, accum-root constant + varying). Validation: 29/29 new tests, 7/7 NifKeyCurveTests, full non-interactive suites green (1519+320+53), format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-05 Done: Ee2KfAnimationImportTests (interactive, 6 tests) lock the 7 DDF-bound EE2 clips through NifAnimationImporter. Descriptor test: all 7 clips import with KF-stem names, table durations (2.1667/1.0/3.0 s), exact channel counts (Galley 20: 12 oars Quaternion-only + ROOT and ROOT NonAccum with TranslationX/Y/Z; Bomber 16: all 4 targets full sets), per-target channel kinds; the unreferenced ab11_TwinEngineBomber.kf fails naming missing target prop_1. Runtime pose tests (headless TestGraphicsContext, no Generals install, ConstantRandom, zero-delta Update to refresh RelativeBoneTransforms): Galley Idle animated offsets stay identity through half the clip; Bomber Walk prop_01 turns 90 degrees (±0.5) between t=0 and t=1/12 s; Bomber TakeOff t=0 equals the rest pose except the root bone, which flight clips key to identity while root NonAccum carries the ground pose (rotation asserted different from rest); Bomber TakeOff 1.333 s root NonAccum world pose equals Walk t=0 pose. Channel structure was verified empirically against the installed archive, then locked. Validation: 6/6 interactive tests, full non-interactive suites green (1519+320+53), format/brace clean.
2026-09-23: WI-C4c-06 Done: Ee2NifProof scenario extended with 8 animated captures per deep dive sec 8 (galley walk 0000/0767/1433, galley idle 0000, bomber walk 0000/0083, bomber takeoff 0000/1333) driven through NifAnimationImporter -> ImportedAnimationMaterializer -> C2 named binding -> PlayToTime before StandaloneModelCapture; outputs ee2-<stem>_<milliseconds>.png plus a guide documenting each frame check. Vision-verified acceptance: oar sweep clearly differs across the three galley walk frames (extended -> horizontal sweep -> recovered), bomber props quarter-turn between walk 0000 and 0083 (diff confined to the two nacelles), takeoff_0000 byte-identical to the static ground pose, takeoff_1333 shows the raised flight attitude with airframe matching walk_0000 (17 px differ), galley idle_0000 == walk_0000 == static (rest pose; single-pixel rounding vs static documented). Determinism: root-caused and fixed a real rendering race — ModelMeshInstance.OnBeforeRender uploads per-mesh world constants inline during pass execution and hardware Vulkan (RADV) can apply them after the draws that read them, so some meshes rendered with stale world matrices (1-4 px displacement, one wires mesh stretched into a 200 px sliver) while CPU pose dumps stayed byte-identical; llvmpipe serializes and never shows it. Fix: StandaloneModelCapture.OnBuildingRenderList now flushes every sub-object's world constant synchronously before the capture passes (WaitForIdle serializes captures); with the fix 4/4 fresh runs produce byte-identical PNG sets on RADV (aggregate md5 99327942fde0471d68a20cbb09c8881a). Proper engine fix (per-frame constant ring) recorded as future work. 3 new Ee2NifProofScenarioTests (animated plan values, file-name stem+padded-ms scheme, guide content incl. determinism note), no GPU needed. C4c marked Done in track + implementation checklist; no EE2 bytes committed. Validation: 9/9 scenario tests, full non-interactive suites green, format/brace clean.
2026-09-23: NIF rotation convention fix (post-C4c bug report): animated-capture review showed the Galley oars crossing under the keel in every frame including the rest pose, root-causing to a C4a static-import error, not the animation pipeline. The stored EE2 nifcache 3x3 is the column-vector rotation map (NifSkope convention); the engine composes row-vector, so the stored->engine hand-off must transpose. C4a's positional copy inverted every non-identity rotation; it survived because hull/root nodes are identity and every lock (Euler byte anchor, propeller turn magnitude, AABBs, captures) was either transpose-blind or self-derived under the inverted convention. Ironic history: card-03's original transposed ToQuaternion was closer to right; card-04 aligned it with CreateLocalMatrix, making the pipeline consistently wrong instead of half-wrong. Fix: NifTransformConverter.CreateLocalMatrix and NifRotationSampler.ToQuaternion now transpose the stored matrix into the row-vector engine layout (EulerToMatrix still returns the stored layout; the byte anchor R_OAR14 to 2e-4 is untouched); determinant/winding and inverse-transpose normals are transpose-invariant. Evidence beyond the fix: scratch dump of the walk KF showed all oars share R_OAR02's quadratic keys, Hermite stays within key extremes under all four tangent conventions, and a full-stroke W2 simulation sweeps outboard (lateral -12.9..-21.5, height -10.5 catch to -3.0 release) — a textbook stroke. Tests updated: spin-direction and XYZ-angle signs flipped; Ee2NifImportTests world AABBs re-derived under the corrected bake (Galley oar beam widens x to +-19.4; Bomber pitch sign flip); C4a storage deep dive corrected (rotation-layout note + new extents) and the C4c deep dive points at it. Validation: 73/73 synthetic NIF tests, 10/10 interactive EE2 (pose asserts are relational and passed unchanged), full non-interactive suites green, format/brace clean, Ee2NifProof repeat run byte-identical; vision-verified captures: oars fan outboard at the gunwale at rest and through the stroke, no shaft under the keel or past the bow, bomber intact and flight pose correct.
